659
00:37:09,680 --> 00:37:13,190
of you and saw that
in your notes--

660
00:37:13,190 --> 00:37:15,747
at runtime, they're not
going to do search anymore.

661
00:37:15,747 --> 00:37:17,330
What they're going
to do at this point

662
00:37:17,330 --> 00:37:20,312
is they're just trying to find
the best possible algorithm.

663
00:37:20,312 --> 00:37:21,770
And then in the
future, they're not

664
00:37:21,770 --> 00:37:24,600
going to do any additional
Monte Carlo tree search,

665
00:37:24,600 --> 00:37:26,582
unlike what we do with plain Go.

666
00:37:26,582 --> 00:37:28,290
Because the assumption
is, at that point,

667
00:37:28,290 --> 00:37:29,290
they have the algorithm.

668
00:37:29,290 --> 00:37:31,470
And they'll just apply
it to multiplying.

669
00:37:31,470 --> 00:37:34,250
So they don't continue to
do Monte Carlo tree search

670
00:37:34,250 --> 00:37:35,640
kind of at runtime.

671
00:37:35,640 --> 00:37:38,840
This is all something done just
to find that best algorithm.

672
00:37:38,840 --> 00:37:42,890
So this is a case where we would
have Monte Carlo tree search,

673
00:37:42,890 --> 00:37:46,230
and we would also
have policy networks.

674
00:37:46,230 --> 00:37:49,370
Policy and value network.

675
00:37:49,370 --> 00:37:50,540
And where they're sharing--

676
00:37:50,540 --> 00:37:53,010
again, this is a
single neural network.

677
00:37:53,010 --> 00:37:54,840
So you can get shared
representations here,

678
00:37:54,840 --> 00:37:57,530
very similar to AlphaZero.

679
00:37:57,530 --> 00:38:00,830
And then they can
play in this case.

680
00:38:00,830 --> 00:38:01,656
Yeah?

